/*  Voidables — `voidable number`, `void`, `but void is`, and narrowing by `is not void`.

    ★ A voidable is `{ has, value }`: `has` is 0 for void. A value goes in WRAPPED — the same
      coercion a union's cases go in by — and comes out by `but void is`, or by narrowing: inside
      `If x is not void`, `x` reads as its value.

    ★ A voidable of a number, a text or a fact is written into every program, ahead of the
      objects, so an object may hold one; a voidable of an object or a union is written with the
      unions, after the objects it holds.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    Bind fact to is-voidable, given (the text kind):
        Return kind starts with "voidable ".
    Done.

    /// What a voidable holds when it is not void.
    Bind text to voidable-inner, given (the text kind):
        Return the characters from 10 to the end of kind.
    Done.

    Bind text to voidable-c-name, given (the text kind):
        Define inner as cast voidable-inner on (kind).
        If cast is-union on (inner), return "cvo_{cast union-c-name on (inner)}".
        If cast object-of on (inner) is not "", return "cvo_obj_{cast c-ident on (cast object-of on (inner))}".
        If cast is-scalar on (inner), return "cvo_{inner}".
        // A series or a map, which a lookup in a map may give.
        Return "cvo_{cast c-tag on (inner)}".
    Done.

    /// A voidable's struct, how one is made, and how it is written and compared.
    Bind text to c-voidable-helpers, given (the text kind):
        Define type-c as cast voidable-c-name on (kind).
        Define inner as cast voidable-inner on (kind).
        Define c-language voidable-struct, given (the term type-c, the c-language axiom held, the term some, the term none,
                the term writer, the c-language axiom written, the term equal, the c-language axiom same),
            as [typedef struct { int has; the held value; } the type-c;
static the type-c the some(the held v) { the type-c o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); o.has = 1; o.value = v; return o; }
static the type-c the none(void) { the type-c o; memset(&o, 0, sizeof o); return o; }
static void the writer(the type-c o) { if (o.has) { the written; } else fputs("void", stdout); }
static int the equal(the type-c a, the type-c b) { if (a.has != b.has) return 0; if (!a.has) return 1; return the same; }

].
        Return voidable-struct on (type-c, cast c-type on (inner), "{type-c}_some", "{type-c}_none", "{type-c}_write",
            cast write-call on (inner, [o.value]), "{type-c}_eq", cast c-equal on (inner, [a.value], [b.value])) converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Every voidable of a number, a text or a fact.
    Bind text to c-voidable-prelude:
        Define out as a chase.
        For each inner in a series of text with ("number", "text", "fact", "bits"), repeat:
            Insert cast c-voidable-helpers on ("voidable {inner}") into out.
        Done.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// A value going into a voidable place: void, wrapped, or as it is.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-into-voidable unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom value, the text source-kind, the text wanted):
        If source-kind is wanted, return value.
        Define type-c as cast voidable-c-name on (wanted).
        If source-kind is "void", return call-of-one on ("{type-c}_none", cast no-c).
        Define inner as cast voidable-inner on (wanted).
        Return call-of-one on ("{type-c}_some", cast one's c-coerce on (value, source-kind, inner)).
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// `<value> but void is <default>` — the value, or the default where it is void; the default
    /// worked out only then.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-but-void unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define held-kind as cast one's kind-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        Define value as cast one's c-of on (held) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-voidable on (held-kind) is false, return value.
        Define inner as cast voidable-inner on (held-kind).
        Define fallback as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), inner) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language or-default, given (the term type-c, the c-language axiom value, the c-language axiom fallback),
            as [({ the type-c cf_v = the value; cf_v.has ? cf_v.value : (the fallback); })].
        Return or-default on (cast voidable-c-name on (held-kind), value, fallback).
    Done.

    Bind text or failure to but-void-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held-kind as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-voidable on (held-kind), return cast voidable-inner on (held-kind).
        Return held-kind.
    Done.

    /// `<value> is void` or `is not void`, either side — a voidable's `has`; anything else is never void.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-void-test unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define tested as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        If tested's kind is "VoidLiteral", the tested becomes cast field-of on (expression, 3).
        Define tested-kind as cast one's kind-of on (tested) or pass the failure off.
        Define is-void as c-verbatim on ([0]).
        If cast is-voidable on (tested-kind):
            Define c-language empty-test, given (the c-language axiom value), as [(!(the value).has)].
            The is-void becomes empty-test on (cast one's c-of on (tested) or pass the failure off).
        Done.
        If (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word is "NotEqual", return negated on (is-void).
        Return is-void.
    Done.

    /// Whether a comparison is with `void`.
    Bind fact to is-void-test, given (the node expression):
        If expression's kind is not "BinaryExpression", return false.
        Define operator as (cast field-of on (expression, 2))'s word.
        If operator is not "Equal" and operator is not "NotEqual", return false.
        Return (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s kind is "VoidLiteral" or (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s kind is "VoidLiteral".
    Done.
Done.
